# Tuscan Butter Gnocchi

Based on [https://www.delish.com/cooking/…](https://www.delish.com/cooking/recipe-ideas/a22845363/tuscan-butter-gnocchi-recipe) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251220074036/https://www.delish.com/cooking/recipe-ideas/a22845363/tuscan-butter-gnocchi-recipe/))

{ rating="5" image="tuscan_butter_gnocchi.jpg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 4 Tbsp [butter]{ ing="butter" }
- [ ] 3 cloves [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, minced
- [ ] 2 cup [halved cherry tomatoes]{ ing="halved-cherry-tomatoes" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [dried oregano]{ ing="dried-oregano" }
- [ ] [Kosher salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" }
- [ ] Freshly [ground black pepper]{ ing="ground-black-pepper" }
- [ ] Pinch [red pepper flakes]{ ing="red-pepper-flakes" }
- [ ] 4 cup [baby spinach]{ ing="baby-spinach" }
- [ ] 1 cup [low-sodium chicken broth]{ ing="low-sodium-chicken-broth" }
- [ ] 1 cup [heavy cream]{ ing="heavy-cream" }
- [ ] 1/2 cup freshly [grated Parmesan]{ ing="grated-parmesan" }
- [ ] 1/4 cup freshly [chopped herbs]{ ing="chopped-herbs" } (such as basil and parsley), plus more for garnish
- [ ] 2 (17.5-oz.) packages [gnocchi]{ ing="gnocchi" }
- [ ] 1 cup [shredded mozzarella]{ ing="shredded-mozzarella" }
- [ ] [Lemon wedges]{ ing="lemon-wedges" }, for serving

## Recipe

1. Preheat oven to 350F
1. In a large skillet over medium heat, melt [butter]{ ing="butter" }. Add [garlic]{ ing="garlic" } and cook until fragrant (1 min)
1. Add [cherry tomatoes]{ ing="halved-cherry-tomatoes" } and season with [oregano]{ ing="dried-oregano" }, [salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" }, [pepper]{ ing="ground-black-pepper" }, and a pinch of [red pepper flakes]{ ing="red-pepper-flakes" }
1. Cook until tomatoes are beginning to burst then add [spinach]{ ing="baby-spinach" } and cook until beginning to wilt
1. Stir in [broth]{ ing="low-sodium-chicken-broth" }, [heavy cream]{ ing="heavy-cream" }, [Parmesan]{ ing="grated-parmesan" }, and [herbs]{ ing="chopped-herbs" }. Bring to a simmer on low heat for about 3 min to reduce the sauce
1. Add [gnocchi]{ ing="gnocchi" } and toss to coat. Pour everything into a 9”-x-13” baking pan and top with [mozzarella]{ ing="shredded-mozzarella" }
1. Bake until gnocchi is cooked through (30 min)
1. Garnish with more herbs and squeeze lemon on top before serving
